\begin{align*}
r_1 + r_2 + r_3 &= -a, \\
r_1r_2 + r_1r_3 + r_2r_3 &= a, \\
r_1r_2r_3 &= -1,
\end{align*}
where $r_1, r_2,$ and $r_3$ are the roots of the cubic equation.
Since all the roots are real, we have:
\begin{align*}
r_1r_2r_3 &= -1 \implies r_1r_2 = -\frac{1}{r_3}, \\
r_1r_2 + r_1r_3 + r_2r_3 &= a \implies -\frac{1}{r_3} + r_1 + r_3 = a, \\
r_1 + r_2 + r_3 &= -a \implies r_2 + r_3 = -a - r_1.
\end{align*}
Substituting $r_2 + r_3 = -a - r_1$ into the second equation, we get:
\begin{align*}
-\frac{1}{r_3} + r_1 + r_3 &= a \\
