 The perimeter of the octagon is equal to the perimeter of the hexagon.

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Perimeter of hexagon} &= 6 \times 16 \text{ cm} \\
&= 96 \text{ cm}
\end{aligned}
\]

Let \( x \) be the side length of the octagon. The perimeter of the octagon is \( 8x \).

\[
\begin{aligned}
8x &= 96 \\
x &= \frac{96}{8} \\
x &= 12
\end{aligned}
\]

Each side of the octagon is 12 cm long.

\boxed{12}

